(Thermal Stress and Recovery of Reef-Building Corals: A Thesis Summary) Tj
T* (Department of Marine Biology - Master of Science thesis, 2025) Tj
T* (Abstract) Tj
T* (This thesis examines how marine heatwaves trigger the breakdown of the symbiosis between) Tj
T* (reef-building corals and their photosynthetic algae \(zooxanthellae, family Symbiodiniaceae\).) Tj
T* (When sea surface temperatures stay about 1 degree C above the summer maximum for several) Tj
T* (weeks, corals expel their algae and turn white. Without the sugars supplied by the algae,) Tj
T* (the coral starves unless temperatures return to normal quickly.) Tj
T* (Methods) Tj
T* (We monitored 42 permanent transects on three reefs between 2019 and 2024. Heat stress was) Tj
T* (measured in degree heating weeks \(DHW\) derived from satellite temperature data. Colonies) Tj
T* (were tagged and photographed every two months, and tissue samples were genotyped to) Tj
T* (identify the dominant symbiont clade.) Tj
T* (Results) Tj
T* (Bleaching began at 4 DHW and mortality rose sharply above 8 DHW. Branching Acropora) Tj
T* (species suffered up to 70 percent mortality, while massive Porites colonies mostly) Tj
T* (recovered within six months. Colonies hosting heat-tolerant Durusdinium symbionts bleached) Tj
T* (less, but grew about 30 percent slower in normal years, suggesting a trade-off.) Tj
T* (Reefs with high herbivorous fish biomass showed faster recovery because grazing kept) Tj
T* (seaweed from overgrowing dead coral skeletons.) Tj
T* (Discussion) Tj
T* (Recurrent heatwaves now arrive every 3 to 6 years, faster than the 10 to 15 years that) Tj
T* (reefs need to recover. Local management - reducing nutrient runoff and protecting grazing) Tj
T* (fish - can buy time, but cannot replace cutting global greenhouse gas emissions.) Tj
T* (Conclusion) Tj
T* (Coral communities are shifting toward slower-growing, stress-tolerant species, with less) Tj
T* (structural complexity and less habitat for reef fish.) Tj
